    ":question/id": "fa39cf5e-b1cf-510a-a444-4f30da1c63f4",
    ":question/math-academy-id": "q-66814",
    ":question/problem": "Given that ${11}^{2x-3}=\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}},$  find the value of $x$ rounded to $3$ decimal places.",
    ":question/worked-solution": "Taking ${log}_{11}$ of both sides of the equation gives:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{11}^{2x-3} & =\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}} \\\\ {log}_{11}\u2061({11}^{2x-3}) & ={log}_{11}\u2061(\\sqrt[3]{{7}^{2}}) \\\\ 2x-3 & ={log}_{11}\u2061({7}^{2/3})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we apply the power rule to the right-hand side:\n\n$$\n2x-3=\\frac{2}{3}{log}_{11}\u2061(7)\n$$\n\nNext, we rewrite the right-hand side using the change of base formula and then solve for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2x-3 & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{log}\u2061(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}\u2061(11)} \\\\ 2x & =\\frac{2\\operatorname{log}\u2061(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}\u2061(11)}+3 \\\\ x & =\\frac{\\operatorname{log}\u2061(7)}{3\\operatorname{log}\u2061(11)}+\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nEvaluating the above on a calculator gives\n\n$$\nx\u22481.771\n$$\n\nrounded to $3$ decimal places."
  }
